# The HV board's new fault HV_UNDERVOLT_ERROR (22, STMBL_FW_VERSION 2): its
# 3.3 V fell below the PVD and TIM8 broke (stm32f303/src/comps/io.c). The
# F4 takes the code as it comes, treats it as an HV board fault (outputs
# off, no stop: the power stage can't be trusted), and names it.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 100
run 0.5
hv0.sim_fault = 22
run 0.004
fault0.stop
run 0.3
fault0.fault
fault0.en_out
@expect fault0.fault == 22
@expect fault0.stop[1] == 0
@expect fault0.en_out == 0
@match HV undervoltage
